## Path 

Open MPI requires to have both files in Identical Path.

We are using PowerShell to logged into WSL enviroment. 
This will loged you into: 
```bash
mpiuser@DESKTOP-RRCLJSQ:/mnt/c/Users/Arham$ 
```

### Why Both Need the File
MPI works by launching the same script on multiple machines. When you run:
```bash
mpirun --hostfile hosts -np 8 python3 mpi_hello.py
```
MPI spawns processes on Laptop A (ranks 0-3) and Laptop B (ranks 4-7). Each machine runs its own copy of ```python3 mpi_hello.py```.

If Laptop B doesn't have the file, its ranks will crash with:
```plain
python3: can't open file '/home/username/mpi_hello.py': [Errno 2] No such file or directory
```
### Solution: Keep Paths Identical
The cleanest approach is to use the same path on both machines:

```bash# Go to your native WSL home directory
cd ~

# Check where you are
pwd
# Should show: /home/GuyThatDoesEveryThin

# Create your project folder here
mkdir -p ~/minihpc
cd ~/minihpc
```

### Hello World!
Create file ```mpi_hello.py``` inside ```minihpc``` folder.
```bash
nano mpi_hello.py
```
Paste this: 
```bash
from mpi4py import MPI

comm = MPI.COMM_WORLD
rank = comm.Get_rank()
size = comm.Get_size()
name = MPI.Get_processor_name()

print(f"Hello from rank {rank} of {size} on {name}")
```

Save: ```Ctrl+O```, ```Enter```, ```Ctrl+X```


### Execute 
Run the above code on single machine 
```bash
mpirun -np 2 python3 mpi_hello.py
```

Expected Output:
```bash
Hello from rank 0 of 4 on DESKTOP-XXX
Hello from rank 1 of 4 on DESKTOP-XXX
```
If get any error, Debug using below guide/

